+4. Perform a Single Radial Immunodiffusion (SRID) assay via a modified Mancini method. Prepare gels using 1.5% agarose in 0.01 M PBS (pH 7.2–7.4) containing 15 µL/mL of monospecific antiserum. Pre-treat standard antigen and test samples with 10% Zwittergent 3-14 detergent (1:10 ratio, 30 min incubation at room temperature), then load 25 µL into each well. Incubate plates in a humid chamber at room temperature. Wash the gels five times in PBS (30–40 min per wash at 40–50 rpm) followed by two washes in distilled water (15 min each), ensuring gels remain completely submerged. Stain with 0.3% Coomassie Brilliant Blue G-250 and destain with an acetic acid-ethanol mixture until precipitation zones are clear. Measure ring diameters and calculate $D^2$ against a calibration curve. Include recombinant human SOD1 (Novus Biologicals Cat. No. NBP2-34940) as a positive control, and OMP16, OMP19, L7/L12, IalB, and BSA as negative/cross-reactivity controls.
 
 5. Validate the SRID assay by evaluating:
-   - Specificity, using target SOD1 dilutions (20, 10, 5 µg/mL and serial dilutions) alongside OMP16, OMP19, L7/L12, IalB, and BSA controls.
